      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Vrchat is a multiplayer environment and has a dedicated streamer community, they're everywhere \n\nThe solution to avoid streamers is to avoid public worlds but at the same time, a majority of streamers also stay in friend/invite only sessions. They also almost-always have block avatars by default, because they don't know you either\n\nBut that's not the real danger, the fact that people will know that they're streaming will paint a huge target on streamers, and toxic people love to harass streamers.\nBy using the Icon, it would be treated as a \"badge of shame\" on streamers with people getting immediately mad at them and spread the mindset that \"it's a streamer, eugh\" or \"there's a streamer here, guys lets leave\", or like when ever you see an account with a twitch url. A lot of streamers are good people and dedicate their times to exploring VRchat and meeting its amazing people, they're still people who want to play the game just like you and I don't think they should target themselves to do that.\n\nIf you're worried about looking bad on a stream or anything, it's the internet, as long as you're not a dick, it'll be fine",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
    {
