      "value": "@{5a570cf1b301553d0104bddd|full_name}: If someone is streaming they are already marked as a streamer because they are streaming live to a platform like twitch which anyone ingame can go and check. Their actions are already affected because they have to be mindful of the TOS on their streaming platform of choice as well. Players target streamers regardless of how they find out. That is a separate issue.\n\nTails as an example is a long time VRC streamer who has always had a marker on their avatar that they are streaming ingame and I've never seen that affect their viewercount or streaming experience.\n\nWhat's more important here is that people are somehow told that they are live on camera. VRC has become a very very social game and it's unfair on those to constantly have to concerned that someone they don't know could be streaming their activities and so they don't have to ask every new person they meet \"are you streaming\". This saves both parties involved time and effort.\n\nThis feature doesn't have to be enforced either. It just has to be there and ready to use so a streamer new to VRchat can simply turn it on in the settings menu rather then spending time adding it to their avatar and all the other annoyances that come along with that.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
