      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "This post is not an indication of work or favoring for/against a feature like this, but just feedback. Additionally, keep in mind I am not a software engineer!\n\nThe only way for us to detect if someone is recording the screen is to analyze the process list on someone's computer. This is invasive and difficult to do without appearing (to malware scanners like Windows Defender) like a malicious piece of software. It is also absurdly complex, and a variation of this technique is used in anti-cheat software that entire companies are dedicated to developing.\n\nIn short, this is a good suggestion, but likely exceedingly difficult to execute.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
